From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] jails: Cache packages on the host across builds
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: rlrnvwpznomnnymxslvlslltypytlrvv
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:56:04 +0000

pkg keeps its cache under the jail root, and a clean build starts from
an empty dataset, so every fresh build fetched every base and ports
package again, over 200 MiB each time. Sharing one cache across
instances and rebuilds makes a clean build cost only the packages that
changed upstream.

The cache is a host directory nullfs-mounted into the root only while
pkg runs, so the running jail never sees or writes it.
---
change-id: rlrnvwpznomnnymxslvlslltypytlrvv
base-branch: b/dev@upstream

This answers "[ISSUE] Building jail instances fetches all the
packages" [1].

Untested: I build from inside lab-claude, which has no zroot/jails
and cannot mount, so I could not run a jail build. sh -n passes, and
I checked that an EXIT trap set inside main still fires when main
fails under the "main | tee" pipeline, which is what unmounts the
cache on an error. The build user needs doas rights for mount and
umount on the host; please check that before applying.

pkg names cached files name-version~hash.pkg, so one directory can
serve every instance, base and ports alike.

